  "verbalization": "Isorosmanol is implicated in the regulation of DNA polymerase iota through a multi-step mechanism involving histone deacetylase 5. The evidence suggests that Isorosmanol acts as a target for Histone deacetylase 5, which in turn targets DNA polymerase iota. This pathway implies a potential role for Isorosmanol in modulating DNA polymerase iota activity, possibly by influencing the acetylation state of histone deacetylase 5. The presence of a second, more complex compound that also targets DNA polymerase iota further supports the idea that Isorosmanol may exert its effects through a similar mechanism, possibly by interacting with the same or a related regulatory pathway. The integration of these findings highlights a potential link between Isorosmanol and DNA polymerase iota, suggesting a possible role in gene regulation or cellular processes involving DNA replication.",
